  "idea": "Async decision documentation framework using Github or Notion RFCs",
  "text": "The best remote companies make critical architectural decisions without ever scheduling a live meeting. Dragging ten engineers across six time zones into one Zoom call leads to endless circular arguments. Worse, verbal agreements vanish from memory, forcing teams to revisit identical technical debates months later. Instituting a formal Request For Comments process inside GitHub Discussions requires authors to document proposals in writing. Decisions get approved asynchronously within two days.",
